gest partisan signal of any state, and with no polls or expert ratings to contradict it, fundamentals alone make this Safe Republican territory.", "watch": "A historically large national Democratic wave or an unusually weak Republican nominee could narrow the margin, though flipping the state remains a remote possibility.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wyoming remains the most Republican-leaning state in the country, with a partisan lean of roughly 23 points toward the GOP. The 2028 race is an open contest because the incumbent president is term-limited, but no candidate or campaign dynamic is likely to overcome the state's deep partisan alignment. No public general-election polls or expert ratings are available for this race, so the forecast rests on the state's fundamental partisanship.\n\nNational headlines point to a somewhat favorable environment for Democrats, with polling elsewhere showing gains amid voter discontent. Even so, a national swing large enough to put Wyoming in play would be historically unprecedented. Republicans enter the race with a cushion that neither candidate selection nor campaign spending has plausibly threatened in recent cycles.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0282, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.025, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0274, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0226, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -23.0}]}